WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.520
A liver cell and a kidney cell carry the same genome.

2
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:11.560
Yet each one reads a different set of genes, and its daughters keep reading the same

3
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:17.420
set. Eukaryotic DNA is packed into chromatin, and packed DNA is hard to read.

4
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:19.280
How does a cell choose?

5
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.260
Part of the answer is a stretch of DNA called an enhancer.

6
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:29.970
An enhancer is DNA that raises transcription from a promoter, at a distance and in

7
00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.010
either orientation.

8
00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:36.530
Transcription factors bind it and recruit coactivators and the Mediator complex.

9
00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:41.050
Mediator links them to RNA polymerase II at the promoter.

10
00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.850
In the usual picture, the DNA between them loops out.

11
00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:50.730
To map one, scientists clone a region beside a promoter that drives luciferase, a

12
00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:56.490
reporter. This region of 600 base pairs holds three elements: A, B, and C.

13
00:00:57.483 --> 00:01:02.543
First, delete each element in turn and test liver cells, with each value a mean of

14
00:01:02.543 --> 00:01:06.903
repeats. Activity is scaled so the promoter alone scores 1.

15
00:01:07.663 --> 00:01:09.343
The full region scores 100.

16
00:01:10.423 --> 00:01:15.323
Delete A, and it still scores 95, so A adds little when B and C are both present.

17
00:01:15.983 --> 00:01:19.943
Delete B, and it falls to 4; delete C, and it falls to 30.

18
00:01:20.967 --> 00:01:22.587
Now test the pieces alone.

19
00:01:23.627 --> 00:01:26.087
B alone scores 5, so B is not sufficient.

20
00:01:27.207 --> 00:01:30.627
C alone scores 2. B and C together score 90.

21
00:01:31.547 --> 00:01:36.047
If their effects added, you would expect about 6; if they multiplied, about 10.

22
00:01:37.047 --> 00:01:41.327
90 is about nine times the multiplied guess, so B and C work together.

23
00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:47.530
Reverse B and C, and it still scores 88, so orientation does not matter here.

24
00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:51.170
Now try kidney cells, where nothing scores above 2.

25
00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:56.370
The simplest reading is that kidney cells lack a factor that B or C needs.

26
00:01:57.230 --> 00:01:58.870
A kidney repressor would also fit.

27
00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:05.853
So of the constructs tested, the minimal liver enhancer is B + C. This fits factors

28
00:02:05.853 --> 00:02:10.193
on both pieces that must be present at once, like a committee that needs the right

29
00:02:10.193 --> 00:02:13.053
members. That is combinatorial control.

30
00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.253
But this is a reporter test.

31
00:02:16.173 --> 00:02:20.533
Its role at the native gene needs a test there, such as deleting B in the genome.
